.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * 
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
. 
.         *       Our operationalization ensures ranodmization of the treatment
>  and hence warrants a causal interpretation. 
.         *       Thus, we do not employ further controls.
.         *       The only exception are survey waves to control for general tr
> ends in gender equality and trends in birth rates. 
.         *       We use a random effects model with observations clustered at 
> the individual level. We xtset our data. We do not use an OLS since a RE mode
> l is more efficient. 
.         
.         * The hypothesis is tested by specifying an interaction between daugh
> ter and sex.
.                 
.         xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2000 to 2020, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         * H4
.         xtreg egal 1.daughter##1.sex i.syear, cluster(pid) re
sex:  factor variables may not contain negative values
